{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305121,"nonce":"dGoK029zF+ZcR2ki7+bNzE9VIvM=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhc2g","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/4","origin":"github"},"title":"Merged output is never verified after writing","message":"`construct_file()` assembles a file from multiple sources and then `shutil.move`s it into place without re-hashing anything.\n\nFor a data-recovery tool the written result should be verified against the piece hashes before being declared good. Verifying on write costs one CPU-bound SHA-1 pass and no extra I/O, since the bytes are already passing through userspace.\n\nWithout it, the offset bugs in the merge path produce corrupt output that reports success.","files":null}]}